   191	## 2. The lift: no round wall for gpt-6-luna runs, one logged 30 min hang guard per call (owner 2026-09-24) (r3 P1-1) (r2 P2-3) (r2 P3-1) (r1 P2-4)
   192	
   193	### 2.1 Where the 180 s bound lives today [V: code read]
   194	
   195	1. `tools/ai-dm-conversation.ts:1265` sets `roundWallMs: 180_000` unconditionally. `tools/ai-dm-arena.ts:423-428` accepts only `--round-wall-ms 180000`, `:685` stores it in `experimentPolicy`, `:97` types it as the literal `180000`, and `:888` passes it into the conversation config.
   196	2. `:5544-5548` builds one `createConversationRoundDeadline(config.roundWallMs, roundStarted, policyNow)` per round.
   197	3. Every agent dispatch goes through that deadline. The primary goes through `lifecycle.coldStartRound(primaryInvocation, roundDeadline)` or `resumeRound` (`:5633`, `:5636`), escalation through `startEscalation(…, deadline)` (`:6190-6203`), speculation through `roundDeadline.dispatch` (`:4826`), and recalculation through `roundDeadline.dispatch` (`:6926`).
   198	4. `src/vtt/agent-session-lifecycle.ts:64-71`: `dispatch()` returns `timeoutMs = Math.min(invocation.timeoutMs ?? remainderMs, remainderMs)` and rewrites the invocation. `:157-158`: the adapter gets `dispatch.invocation` and `deadline.signal`, which aborts at the wall (`:52-61`).
   199	5. So a primary call is killed at the remaining round budget (≤ 180 s), whatever `--timeout-ms` says. r3's claim "the round wall does not abort the primary session" was wrong; Appendix E item 1 records how.
   200	6. In blind mode the runner also sends the engine a per-round deadline, `blindDeadlineUnixMs = Date.now() + config.timeoutMs` (`:4534`), reused by the correction launcher (`:5848`). The engine refuses late blind submissions (`engine-server.ts:2363`). `:7339` derives the attempt timing baseline as `blindDeadlineUnixMs - config.timeoutMs`.
