   202	**Finding against the records (for the supervisor).** Part A :430 and :568 say D569 comparisons run at 240 s. The shared 180 s round deadline arrived in `89c2ee31` (2026-09-09 02:15). The v5 launch commit `90484d45` maps to `7d5b5d1b` in `.claude/consensus/purge-2026-09-17-commit-map.txt` (2026-09-09 01:07), and `89c2ee31` is **not** its ancestor [V: `git merge-base --is-ancestor`]. So v5's first arm ran with an effective 240 s, but any dm-mode run on today's main is capped at 180 s. A v5 relaunch would have been silently tighter than registered. v5 is superseded (§6.1), so this matters only for how v7 and the study are registered.
