   219	### 2.3 Mechanism (B1)
   220	
   221	**Resolver** (`tools/model-routes.ts`):
   222	
   223	```ts
   224	resolveSessionBounds({ routes, path, explicitTimeoutMs, explicitRoundWall }):
   225	  // routes: readonly { model: string; effort: string }[]; path: 'legacy' | 'dm_mode'
   226	  // explicitTimeoutMs: number | null; explicitRoundWall: null | 180000   ('none' added in B3b if Q4c = yes)
   227	  luna = routes.filter(r => r.model === LUNA_MODEL).length
   228	  if luna === 0:  return { timeoutMs: explicitTimeoutMs ?? (path === 'dm_mode' ? 240_000 : 120_000),
   229	                           roundWallMs: 180_000,
   230	                           bound: explicitTimeoutMs === null ? 'legacy_default' : 'cli_override' }
   231	  if luna !== routes.length: throw mixed-route refusal
   232	  if explicitTimeoutMs !== null && explicitTimeoutMs !== LUNA_HANG_GUARD_MS: throw lift refusal (names model, effort, value)
   233	  if explicitRoundWall !== null: throw lift refusal (names --round-wall-ms)
   234	  return { timeoutMs: LUNA_HANG_GUARD_MS, roundWallMs: null, bound: 'luna_hang_guard' }
   235	```
   236	
   237	The non-Luna branch returns what the parsers compute today, byte for byte (`ai-dm-conversation.ts:1264`, `ai-dm-arena.ts:675`). `bound` is **not stored on any config**: T6 compares whole configs (`ai-dm-legacy-invariance.test.ts:1278-1294`) [V], and the existing arena test at `ai-dm-arena.test.ts:960-963` asserts `parsed.experimentPolicy` with `toEqual({ roundWallMs: 180_000, basisDirectory })` [V]. The lift is therefore encoded only by `roundWallMs: null` plus `timeoutMs: 1_800_000`; no config gains a field. Only the launcher's provenance records `bound` (§5).
   238	
   239	`resolveScreenshotTimeout({ model, explicitTimeoutMs })`: gpt-6-luna → 1,800,000 (an explicit value must equal it); any other model → `explicitTimeoutMs ?? null` (null = untimed, as today).
   240	
   241	**Unbounded deadline** (`src/vtt/agent-session-lifecycle.ts`):
   242	
   243	```ts
   244	export function createUnboundedRoundDeadline(): AgentDispatchDeadline {
   245	  const signal = new AbortController().signal;          // never aborted, no timer
   246	  return {
   247	    signal,
   248	    dispatch(invocation) {
   249	      if (invocation.timeoutMs === undefined) throw new RangeError('An unbounded round requires a per-call hang guard.');
   250	      return { kind: 'open', timeoutMs: invocation.timeoutMs, invocation };
   251	    },
   252	    acceptsCompletion: () => true,
   253	  };
   254	}
   255	```
   256	
   257	A huge number in place of `null` was rejected. `createConversationRoundDeadline` re-arms `setTimeout(scheduleAbort, Math.ceil(remainderMs))` (`:58`), and Node clamps delays above 2,147,483,647 ms to 1 ms [I: Node timers documentation], which would give a 1 ms re-arm loop. A 30 min *round* wall was also rejected, because D890 asks for a per-call guard: a round has several calls (initial, corrections, adjustments, escalation).
