   290	
   291	## 3. The effort study: gpt-6-luna high vs xhigh picks the route (owner 2026-09-24)
   292	
   293	### 3.1 Design (pre-stated here; copied verbatim into the S-PREREG D-entry before any study cell runs)
   294	
   295	- **Id** `luna6-effort-study-v1`. **Question:** does gpt-6-luna at xhigh beat gpt-6-luna at high on D569-scored decision quality by more than δ, and at what cost in response time per call?
   296	- **Arms:** `gpt-6-luna-high` (model `gpt-6-luna`, effort `high`) and `gpt-6-luna-xhigh` (model `gpt-6-luna`, effort `xhigh`). Both are lifted (§2): 1,800,000 ms per call, no round wall, no engine blind deadline.
   297	- **Same states:** the D569 v5 primary cohorts, carried from the v5 manifest [V]: `evaluation-hard` seeds 5117001–5117010 (`tests/fixtures/arena-basis-hard/seed-*.json`, shas in the manifest) and `evaluation-brutal` seeds 6203001–6203010 (`tests/fixtures/arena-basis-brutal/seed-*.json`). 3 reps; each cell is one fresh round on the fixture's starting state, identical for both arms.
   298	- **Modes:** blind (`--dm-mode blind --blind-repair-arm code_only --blind-facts off`, 3 attempts) and advice (`--dm-mode advice`). Settings otherwise follow the v5 manifest's `execution` block [V]: `freshSessionPerCell true, escalation false, modelDefaultFallback false, transport mcp_minimal, boardImage png`; KB `tests/fixtures/ai-dm-kb/d569/ai-dm-core.md`; caps 65 536 / 8 192 / 32 768.
   299	- **Cells:** 2 arms × 2 modes × 2 bases × 10 seeds × 3 reps = **240**, run as 8 arena invocations of 30 cells, in the fixed ABBA order hard-blind (high, xhigh), hard-advice (xhigh, high), brutal-blind (xhigh, high), brutal-advice (high, xhigh), on a quiet box (D883; D890: no agent tests during runs).
   300	- **Void rule:** more than 3 `infrastructure_failed` cells in a 30-cell block voids that block. It is rerun once in full before any packet is built. A second void STOPs the study and goes to the owner.
   301	- **Scoring, as D569 scores its arms** (`tools/d569-v5/analyze-primary-pair.ts`; `tools/d569-blind-experiment.ts:1030-1122`) [V]:
   302	  - Relabel-only rows carry the arm id. One packet per (mode, basis) holds exactly the two arms paired by (seed, rep), 60 entries each and 240 in total, built by `tools/ai-dm-rerun-packet.ts` with `--protocol r1-10` (hard) or `--protocol brutal-10 --reps 3` (brutal). The builder partitions arms by the row's `arm` field (`:925`, `:1018-1035`) [V], so two gpt-6-luna arms pair correctly.
   303	  - Four packet shuffle seeds are drawn by the supervisor and recorded in S-PREREG; `569575` is not reused.
   304	  - A leak scan runs before judging (V15).
   305	  - The Opus 4.8 notes-only advisory stage runs first, then the three scoring seats `claude-fable-5-1`, `gpt-6-astra` and `gpt-5.6-sol`, each at high in a fresh context (D578.3).
   306	  - Components: targetPriority 0–3, actionEconomy 0–3, coherence 0–2, positioning 0–2; total 0–10.
   307	  - A cell's panel value is the sum over components of the mean across seats. Refused, execution_failed and service_failed cells score 0 (zero-inclusive). `infrastructure_failed` is excluded pairwise.
   308	  - **A cell whose call log has `hangGuardFired: true` is scored 0 whatever the runner classified it as, and is never excluded.**
   309	
   310	### 3.2 Decision rule and the named test
   311	
   312	- **Estimand.** Δ = the mean, over all complete pairs pooled across both modes and both bases, of (xhigh − high) zero-inclusive panel totals.
   313	- **Test: one-sided cluster-bootstrap percentile test of superiority by margin δ = 0.20 at α = 0.025.** H0: Δ ≤ 0.20 against H1: Δ > 0.20.
   314	  - Clusters are encounter seeds: 20 clusters (10 hard, 10 brutal), each holding its 6 paired differences (2 modes × 3 reps).
   315	  - 100,000 resamples with the D569 generator and percentile rule (mulberry32, `index = floor(q·n)` clamped to `[0, n−1]`; `d569-blind-experiment.ts:988-1028`) [V], seed **20260924**.
   316	  - Reject H0 iff the 2.5th percentile of the bootstrap distribution of Δ is > 0.20.
   317	- **Co-condition (as D569's success label, `:976-986`).** The refusal-risk difference (xhigh − high, refused or execution_failed = 1) has a cluster-bootstrap 97.5th percentile ≤ 0.00 (`D569_REFUSAL_RISK_MARGIN`, `:31`), with seed 20260924 + 300.
   318	- **Decision:** E = **xhigh** iff H0 is rejected **and** the co-condition holds; otherwise E = **high**. The burden is on xhigh, as D890 (c) says.
   319	- **Why δ = 0.20.** It is the magnitude D569 registers as its noninferiority margin (`D569_NONINFERIORITY_MARGIN = -0.20`, `:30`) [V], the largest difference D569 treats as negligible. xhigh must be better by more than what the project's registered experiment calls negligible. The margin is fixed now, before any data.
   320	- **One look.** A single analysis runs after all 240 cells are judged. There is no interim look, and no cell is rerun to change the decision.
   321	- **Secondary, reported and not deciding:** Δ per mode and per basis with intervals; the executed-only Δ; per-component Δ; per-seat diagnostics (`analyzeD569DiagnosticPair`).
   322	- **Power is not claimed.** No gpt-6-luna panel-score variance exists locally [I]. An inconclusive interval falls to E = high by construction, and S-RESULT reports the interval so the owner sees how close it was.
   323	
   324	### 3.3 Speed measures (reported, not deciding)
   325	
   326	From the call logs (§2.4), per arm × mode:
   327	- the number of calls;
   328	- p50 / p90 / p95 / max of `elapsedMs`, by nearest rank `ceil(q·n)`;
   329	- the number of calls over 180 000 ms (which the old wall would have censored);
   330	- the number of `hangGuardFired` records.
   331	
   332	Per paired cell: the median of `sum(xhigh elapsed) / sum(high elapsed)`. Reasoning and output tokens come from the rows' `callUsage` (`src/vtt/agent-session.ts:61-70`) [V]. The study reports quality and speed side by side, but only §3.2 decides.
   333	
   334	### 3.4 Freeze sequence (no step consumes a later step's output)
   335	
   336	| Step | Who | Output | Consumes |
   337	|---|---|---|---|
   338	| S-PREREG | supervisor | D-entry: §3.1–§3.3 verbatim, the four shuffle seeds, the call-log schema, installed script shas | this plan |
   339	| B6 | implementer | study code and T8, with constants typed from S-PREREG | S-PREREG |
   340	| Phase S runs | supervisor | 240 rows plus call logs under `~/dnd-slim-runs/luna6-effort/` | B1 and B6 landed |
   341	| Packets, judging | supervisor | 4 packets, keys, normalized seat scores | runs |
   342	| S-RESULT | supervisor | D-entry: E, Δ with interval, co-condition, every secondary and speed number, every hang-guard firing | the analysis operator's output |
   343	
   344	### 3.5 Cost and wall
   345	
   346	- **Model wall** [I; node]: if high ≈ gpt-5.6-luna high's screening median of 162.1 s per cell and xhigh is 1.5× to 2× that, then 120 × 162.1 = 19,452 s for high plus 29,178 to 38,904 s for xhigh, **13.5 to 16.2 h serial**. The ceiling at the hang guard is 240 × 1,800 s = 120 h (a bound, not an estimate). Advice cells may make up to 3 dispatch attempts plus corrections, so more calls than cells.
   347	- **Judging**: 240 entries × (the Opus notes stage + 3 seats). No local cost figure exists for this [I].
   348	- Codex usage is plan-billed (D381: spend is a non-constraint). If Fable is exhausted, the study STOPs loudly with no substitute (K9).
   349	
   350	### 3.6 Until the study reports (PR6)
   351	
   352	S-RESULT gates:
   353	- B5 (the launcher, whose route literal is E);
   354	- B3a/B3b (v7 at E);
   355	- every (a) run on gpt-6-luna.
   356	
   357	Nothing else waits for it: B1, B4, B2 and B6 proceed. A script-chosen run needed before S-RESULT uses today's gpt-5.6-luna route, un-lifted.
   358	
   359	### 3.7 What the study can and cannot say
   360	
   361	It measures route quality on 20 fixed encounters in D569's two decision modes, under D569's panel. It does not measure live-play pacing (speculation is off in dm modes: `:4706`, `if (config.dmModeExplicit) return;`) [V], the screenshot gates, or DATA-01's labelling task. Applying E to those roles follows from D890 (c) ("picks the route for script-chosen Luna runs"), not from their own measurement. gpt-5.6-luna vs gpt-6-luna is not compared.
