   385	### 4.2 Mutation procedure (Part A :88-89; D890) (r3 P1-3) (r1 P1-4)
   386	
   387	Each distinct mutation runs on a clean checkout of the candidate SHA under `PhpstormProjects`, never during a gate on that tree. Every heavy command goes through `/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/perf-02/fanout/slot.sh <clone> …`. The harness is `.tmp/runs/luna6/impl/<batch>/mutate.mjs <id>`, and it exits non-zero on **any** deviation from these steps:
   388	
   389	1. Record the target's sha256 (ORIG). For an untracked (new) file, also write an explicit byte backup.
   390	2. **Killers pass unmutated.** For each named killer (file plus full title, regex-escaped for `-t`): `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --configLoader runner --maxWorkers=1 <file> -t '<escaped title>' --reporter=json`. Require exit 0, exactly one test run and passed, and none skipped. A command killer (M57) must return its stated unmutated result.
   391	3. Apply an exact-string replacement that matches **exactly once**. Print `CHANGED <file>:<line>: <old> -> <new> (1)`.
   392	4. `npx tsc -b --force` (the full project build, which includes test files; not `tsconfig.app.json` alone, not tsgo) must exit 0. A mutant that fails to compile is a **compile control**, never a kill. The harness exits non-zero unless the plan lists that id as a compile control, and this plan lists none.
   393	5. **Killers fail mutated.** Run each named killer again, teed to `<id>.<n>.log`. The harness enforces the predicted failure set: every named killer must fail (non-zero exit, that title listed as failed, and a diff, violation list or designed refusal message containing the mutated value). A crash, import error, timeout or skip is not a kill. The predicted set is exactly the named killers, because each run is filtered to one title.
   394	6. Restore the exact bytes, require sha256 = ORIG, and print `RESTORED <sha>`.
   395	7. **Killers pass again.** Re-run each named killer on the restored bytes and require step 2's result.
   396	
   397	Counts are of **distinct mutations**, not killer rows. The implementer runs all of them and the supervisor re-runs them; kill evidence is read from the logs. **Outcome-as-data:** a new test that probes a path that can throw records each case as `{ ok: value }` or `{ error: message }` and asserts the whole list with `toEqual`, so flipping refusal and acceptance shows up as a diff.
