   596	**T8 (B6), hand-derived expectations.**
   597	- *Clusters:* two hard seeds; seed A's 6 differences are all 1.0 and seed B's all 0.0. With seed clustering, each bootstrap draw is the mean of 2 clusters drawn with replacement, so P(draw = 0) = P(draw = 1) = 1/4 > 2.5 %. The 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles are therefore exactly 0 and 1: `{ lower: 0, upper: 1 }`. Resampling the 12 cells gives P(all 0) = 2⁻¹², so the lower bound is > 0 (M62).
   598	- *Decision:* four synthetic datasets of 20 clusters × 6 pairs, asserted as `['xhigh', 'high', 'high', 'high']`:
   599	  1. every pair +0.5: every bootstrap draw is 0.5, so the lower bound is 0.5 → `'xhigh'`;
   600	  2. every pair +0.1 → `'high'` (M58, margin 0, flips it);
   601	  3. in every cluster, 5 pairs at +0.5 and 1 pair where the xhigh cell is refused and its high partner is executed with all components 0 (difference 0): every draw is 0.4167, but the refusal-risk difference is 1/6 in every cluster, so its 97.5th percentile is 1/6 > 0 → `'high'` (M60, co-condition dropped, flips it);
   602	  4. 10 clusters at +0.8 and 10 at −0.3 (mean 0.25): a draw's mean is (1.1X − 6)/20 with X ~ Bin(20, ½), and P(X ≤ 9) = 0.41 ≫ 0.025, so the 2.5th percentile is ≤ 0.2 → `'high'` (M59, mean in place of the lower bound, flips it to `'xhigh'`).
   603	
   604	  Every value is derivable by hand, without the code under test.
   605	- *Hang-guard kill:* one cell `infrastructure_failed` with call-log `hangGuardFired: true` is scored `{ value: 0, excluded: false }`.
   606	- *Latency:* elapsed values `[10,20,…,200]` (n = 20). Nearest rank gives p50 = 100 (rank 10), p90 = 180 (rank 18), p95 = 190 (rank 19), max = 200. `floor(q·n)` indexing gives 110 / 190 / 200 / 200 (M63).
   607	- *Grid:* 239 rows are refused with the missing cell named (M67).
