   878	
   879	- **Q4a (before B3; yes/no).** "v7 is built from the v5 bytes: it carries v5's cohorts (hard 5117001–5117010, brutal 6203001–6203010), second family and caps unchanged, and records that this supersedes Part A :560/:568 ('active cohorts/caps obey COHORT v6') for v7 only, because COHORT v6 exists only on the shelved `claude/cohort-01` branch. Yes, or no (then v7 is not registered under this plan)?" *Recommendation: yes.* It follows D886 §12b's precedent of running on main's baseline rather than waiting behind the shelved lane. (r3 P1-2)
   880	- **Q4c (before B3; yes/no).** "D890 makes every gpt-6-luna call uncensored (30 min guard, no round wall). Should v7's non-Luna arms (Opus 4.8, Sol, Astra) get the same bound, so that every arm runs under one wall as in v5? If no, v7 cannot be registered under this plan, because its single `experimentWallMs` cannot express per-arm walls." *Recommendation: yes.* A common wall was v5's fairness rule. v5's 240 s was effective when it launched, and today's 180 s round deadline would otherwise censor the judge arms but not Luna (§2.1 finding).
