## D887+D890 scope

Plan r4 does not implement exactly the governing scope.

| Reading | Assessment |
|---|---|
| PR4 — escalation uses E | The base reading is correct ([plan-r4.md:48](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r4.md:48)). Q-ESC unnecessarily reopens it after D890 already says the study picks the script-chosen route ([plan-r4.md:883](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r4.md:883)). |
| PR5 — quality gates use E | Correct ([plan-r4.md:49](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r4.md:49)). |
| PR6 — today’s route until S-RESULT | The role-specific gpt-5.6-luna model/effort reading is reasonable, but keeping it unlifted is not. D890 removes the wall for “Luna runs,” not merely future gpt-6-luna runs. |
| PR7 — lift only all-gpt-6-luna runs | Incorrect. It excludes current gpt-5.6-luna runs ([plan-r4.md:51](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r4.md:51)) and adds an unauthorized refusal for mixed-model runs ([plan-r4.md:212](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r4.md:212)). |
